+## Credential and state handling
+
+Secrets Manager entries use a seven-day deletion recovery window, so an
+accidental Terraform removal is not immediately permanent. Terraform state
+still contains generated values such as the database password, dashboard
+token, encryption roots and assembled database URL. Treat the remote state
+bucket and any local state/cache files as secret-equivalent; access must be
+limited to the deployment principals and protected backups. The bucket is
+versioned and SSE-encrypted with public access blocked, but this document does
+not verify its IAM policy or an AWS deployment.
+
