+## Public form recovery
+
+Form submissions remain in their append-only queue while their current target
+is unavailable. The owner-scoped
+`GET /api/v1/event-triggers/{name}/form-submissions` response includes the
+waiting count and, when a newer release of the same flow is available or a
+legacy form has no valid pinned template, a `rebind_target` for the current
+workflow or template. It includes `kind` (`flow` or `template`), readable
+fields and an opaque release value. The owner can request the matching operation with
+`POST /api/v1/event-triggers/{name}/form-submissions/rebind`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "expected_target_kind": "flow",
+  "expected_generation": "<binding value from the review>",
+  "expected_release_id": "<release value from rebind_target>",
+  "expected_waiting_total": 3
+}
+```
+
+`expected_target_kind` may be `flow` or `template`; it defaults to `flow` for
+existing clients. The reviewed kind, target and waiting-answer count must still
+match exactly when the owner confirms.
+The server rechecks the complete waiting queue, current owner, target release,
+answer compatibility and prior admissions while serializing the change with
+form submission and polling. If any answer no longer fits, or any answer may
+already have started, the request refuses without moving the queue. A successful
+change writes a signed receipt bound to every routed sequence and answer
+fingerprint and accepted version; delivery verifies that receipt before starting
+the workflow or rendering the template. Use
+`GET /api/v1/event-triggers/{name}/form-submissions/rebind-receipt` with the
+original `source_generation`, `target_release_id` and
+`expected_waiting_total` query values to confirm an uncertain response. Include
+`target_kind=template` when confirming a template repair. Previously accepted
+incompatible answers remain held for a separate owner-reviewed repair path.
+
